# No code jargon in user-facing copy

All visible text on the Tralee Masjid site is for mosque visitors, not developers. Write in plain, welcoming language.

## Applies to

- Page headings, leads, buttons, labels, empty states, and error messages
- `aria-label` and other accessibility text read aloud to visitors
- Alt text and link text

Does **not** apply to HTML class names, CSS selectors, JS identifiers, or build tooling.

## Avoid in visitor copy

| Jargon | Prefer instead |
|--------|----------------|
| card | programme, notice, section, entry |
| modal / dialog | details, full information |
| embed / widget | live player, map, donation form |
| toggle | setting, switch, on/off |
| grid / carousel | schedule, list, gallery |
| tab / dropdown | menu, section |
| cache / API / localStorage | (omit — never mention) |
| component | section, block |

## Keep when meant literally

- **Card payment** / **credit card** — payment method, not UI
- **Twitter Card** — meta tag only, not visible copy

## Examples

```html
<!-- BAD -->
<p>Open any card for times and venue.</p>
<p>Enable third-party embeds to load the stream.</p>

<!-- GOOD -->
<p>Tap any programme below for times, speaker, and venue.</p>
<p>Allow external content in Privacy &amp; cookies to listen live.</p>
```

When editing existing pages, scan for jargon and replace with visitor-friendly wording.
